    <h1>About</h1>
  </div>
  <div class="about-body">
    <p>I’m Neil Kodner, a photographer based in Los Gatos, California.</p>
    <p>Hockey is a major part of my photography. Away from the rink, I photograph cities and the people in them.</p>
    <p>I’m looking for editorial assignments and team or league media work, in hockey above all.</p>

    <section class="about-more" aria-labelledby="building">
      <h2 id="building">Building for photographers</h2>
      <p>I photograph hockey and other fast action, often shooting long bursts with my Sony a1 II. A game can leave me with a couple thousand frames to sort through. I wanted a faster way to review them, so I built a Mac app for my own use. That became Palomino.</p>
      <p>It reads the JPEG preview already embedded in each RAW file, so there’s virtually no wait between frames. I can rate and reject photos from the keyboard, then bring the keepers into Lightroom. It doesn’t make the choices for me. It just makes reviewing every frame fast enough that I can still do it myself.</p>
      <p>Palomino runs locally on the Mac, costs a one-time fee, and has no subscription. Other photographers are using it too. You can find it at <a href="https://palomino-app.com">palomino-app.com</a>.</p>
    </section>

